X.append(('g-x-platforms', 'Crosswalk — Platforms and Onboarding',
"The seventh table is where a word-for-word translation misleads most. Stripe documents one account for a seller; Adyen documents several resources that separate identity, permissions and money. The pairing is this book's mapping: neither company publishes a translation to the other ([[platform-payment-models]], [[splits-balances-and-platform-payouts]], [[platform-onboarding-and-verification]]).",
[
('The platform product', 'Connect', 'Adyen for Platforms, with two integration models: marketplace and platform', "Adyen's two models answer who the merchant is before any account exists; only the platform model supports in-person payments.", ['platform-payment-models'], 'ch', ['Connect (Stripe)', 'Adyen for Platforms', 'Marketplace model (Adyen)', 'Platform model (Adyen)']),
('What represents a seller', 'Connected account: one account that carries identity, capabilities, requirements and, through its balance, the funds', 'Four resources: a legal entity (who the seller is), an account holder (what it may do), a balance account (its money) and a transfer instrument (its bank account); a store fixes the name the payer sees. Adyen calls the seller a “user”', '**No one-to-one match.** A connected account is not an account holder and not a balance account: it is all of them at once. One Adyen seller can have several account holders and balance accounts.', ['platform-payment-models'], 'ch', ['Connected account (Stripe)', 'Legal entity (Adyen)', 'Account holder (Adyen)', 'Balance account (Adyen)', 'User (Adyen: seller)']),
("Where the platform's own money sits", 'The platform balance, with a `connect_reserved` part', 'Liable balance account, under the liable account holder; plus a reserved compensation account and a reserved incorrect splits account', "On Adyen the liable accounts are created by Adyen and stand behind every seller by default.", ['platform-payment-models'], 'ch', ['Liable balance account (Adyen)', 'Liable account holder (Adyen)', 'connect_reserved (Stripe)', 'Reserved compensation account (Adyen)']),
('Where the money is kept', "Balances of the platform account and the connected accounts", 'The balance platform: “an accounting system that manages the flow of funds within your business”, separate from the merchant accounts and one per region', 'Adyen names the layer; Stripe does not.', ['platform-payment-models', 'licences-and-safeguarding'], 'ch', ['Balance platform (Adyen)']),
('How a payment is tied to the merchant', 'Charge type and `on_behalf_of`, per payment', 'The integration model, the store and the merchant account', 'Divided differently: per payment at Stripe, by structure at Adyen.', ['platform-payment-models'], 'ch', ['on_behalf_of (Stripe)']),
('How a payment is divided', 'Charge type: a direct charge on the connected account, or a destination charge or separate charges and transfers on the platform', 'A `splits` array of typed bookings on the payment or capture (`BalanceAccount`, `Commission`, `PaymentFee`, `VAT`), or a split configuration profile on the store', "An Adyen split that names a wrong or closed account is booked to the liable balance account without an error; a Stripe transfer that cannot be made fails and is not retried.", ['splits-balances-and-platform-payouts', 'journey-platform-payment'], 'ch', ['Charge type (Stripe)', 'Direct charge (Stripe)', 'Destination charge (Stripe)', 'Separate charges and transfers (Stripe)', 'splits (Adyen)', 'Split configuration profile (Adyen)']),
("The platform's cut", 'Application fee (`application_fee_amount`)', 'Commission (a `Commission` split)', 'Same function.', ['splits-balances-and-platform-payouts'], 'ch', ['Application fee (Stripe)', 'Commission (Adyen)']),
('Moving money between two balances', 'Transfer (and transfer reversal)', 'Internal transfer between balance accounts', "**“Transfer” is a false friend.** At Adyen a payout to a bank account is also a transfer, with its own statuses.", ['splits-balances-and-platform-payouts', 'payouts-and-money-movement'], 'ch', ['Transfer (Stripe and Adyen senses)', 'Internal transfer (Adyen)']),
("Who stands behind a seller's negative balance", '`losses_collector` on the account: `stripe` or `application` (the platform); it cannot be changed later', "The platform's liable accounts by default; a negative balance is allowed for up to 30 days, then the reserved compensation account is debited", 'Stripe documents a provider-borne loss as a per-account setting, Adyen as a pilot (next row).', ['platform-payment-models', 'splits-balances-and-platform-payouts'], 'ch', ['losses_collector (Stripe)']),
('Managed Risk', "The service through which Stripe's risk teams handle seller risk where Stripe is responsible for losses", 'A pilot with limited availability under which Adyen will “assume the responsibility for negative balances” and write them off after 180 days', 'Same name at both, for a provider taking the seller\'s risk; the conditions and availability differ.', ['platform-payment-models', 'splits-balances-and-platform-payouts'], 'ch', ['Managed Risk (Stripe and Adyen senses)']),
('Where a chargeback is booked', 'By charge type: the connected account for direct charges, the platform otherwise', 'By `platformChargebackLogic` sent with the payment (`deductFromLiableAccount`, `deductFromOneBalanceAccount`, `deductAccordingToSplitRatio`); the default is the liable balance account', 'On Adyen the instruction is written before any chargeback exists, so store what you sent with every payment.', ['platform-payment-models', 'journey-dispute'], 'ch', ['platformChargebackLogic (Adyen)']),
('A refund after the seller was paid', '`reverse_transfer` and `refund_application_fee` on the refund', 'A `splits` instruction on the refund; refunds can only be deducted from the balance accounts the payment was credited to', 'Decide who funds a refund before the first late one.', ['journey-platform-payment', 'splits-balances-and-platform-payouts'], 'ch', ['reverse_transfer (Stripe)']),
('A permission on a seller account', 'Capability, with a `status` such as `active`', 'Capability, with `requested`, `allowed`, `enabled` and a `verificationStatus`', 'Same word. On Adyen `enabled` is the platform\'s own switch: a capability can be used only when it is both allowed and enabled.', ['platform-onboarding-and-verification', 'payment-compliance-and-regulation'], 'ch', ['verificationStatus (Adyen)']),
('What is still missing for verification', '`requirements` lists: `currently_due`, `eventually_due`, `past_due`, `pending_verification`, with one `current_deadline`', 'Verification errors with remediating actions per capability; a deadline per capability', 'Stripe says what is missing; Adyen says what is allowed and why not.', ['payment-compliance-and-regulation', 'platform-onboarding-and-verification'], 'ch', ['currently_due (Stripe)', 'requirements (Stripe)', 'Verification errors (Adyen)', 'Remediating actions (Adyen)']),
('Announced changes to requirements', '`future_requirements`, with the date entries move to `requirements`', NONE + ' as an API structure; changes appear in dated release notes', 'On Adyen a rule change shows up as new verification errors.', ['payment-compliance-and-regulation'], 'ch', ['future_requirements (Stripe)']),
('Periodic re-verification', 'KYC Refresh: announced; attestation requirements in `requirements`, API in private preview in 2026', 'A data review: error 3_10 with a deadline, closed by a confirmation call', 'Neither publishes an interval.', ['payment-compliance-and-regulation'], 'ch', ['KYC Refresh (Stripe)', 'Data review (Adyen)']),
('Ways to collect verification data', 'Hosted (an Account Link), embedded (an onboarding component opened with an AccountSession) and API', 'Hosted onboarding (a link, on invite or API-initiated) and API-only; components that “only cover certain functionality”', 'Stripe lets a platform collect by API only when it bears seller losses and sellers have no Stripe dashboard.', ['platform-onboarding-and-verification'], 'ch', ['Account Link (Stripe)', 'AccountSession (Stripe)', 'Hosted onboarding (Adyen)']),
('Kinds of seller account', 'Formerly account types (Standard, Express, Custom; deprecated); in Accounts v2, configurations, responsibilities and a dashboard setting', NONE + ' for an account type; the choice is the integration model and per-payment instructions', "Larkfield's Stripe studios are legacy Custom accounts. A Stripe account's responsibilities cannot be changed after creation.", ['platform-payment-models'], 'ch', ['Accounts v2 (Stripe)', 'Custom account (Stripe)', 'Express account (Stripe)', 'Standard account (Stripe)']),
("An account that keeps a seller's balance", 'Financial account (Treasury); “Stripe is not a bank”, deposits sit at a partner bank', 'Business account: a deposit at Adyen N.V.', 'The license behind the product differs; availability is narrow at both as of November 2026.', ['embedded-finance', 'licences-and-safeguarding'], 'ch', ['Financial account (Stripe)', 'Treasury (Stripe)', 'Business account (Adyen)']),
('Cards and financing for sellers', 'Issuing; Capital (partner lenders)', 'Issuing (a payment instrument on a balance account); Capital (Adyen lends)', 'Same product names. Both give your server about two seconds to answer an issuing authorization.', ['embedded-finance'], 'ch', ['Issuing (Stripe and Adyen)', 'Capital (Stripe and Adyen)', 'Payment instrument (Adyen)']),
]))

